{
 "_readme": "Duplicate records folded together: {keep_id: [drop_ids]}. The keeper takes the union of shelves, keeps its own field values, fills gaps from the dropped record, and inherits its sources. Merging is a curated decision, never automatic — importers/audit_shelves.py prints same-name-nearby CANDIDATES (221 pairs as of 2026-08-07), but a restaurant inside its hotel or two branches of one chain on one soi are separate records. Only pairs a person has looked at belong here.  2026-09-05: 233 register/crawl pairs were folded in one pass under a written rule rather than one at a time — the two records carry the SAME name character for character, NO third record in the province answers to that name, and they stand within 300 m of each other. The rule is the whole argument: where any one of the three held, the pair was left out and written to cache/dupes_needs_eyes.txt instead. 112 pairs are there now, 70 because the names differ by an abbreviation or a space and 42 because a third record shares the name — both are the case a loose join gets wrong, and neither is settled from a desk.",
